{"name":"Fiery Brown","hex":"#5d3831","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fiery","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to fire.","Burning or glowing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fiery"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fire","blocks":[{"text":"Fire is the rapid oxidation of a fuel in the exothermic chemical process of combustion, releasing heat, light, and various reaction products.\nFlames, the most visible portion of the fire, are produced in the combustion reaction when the fuel reaches its ignition point temperature. Flames from hydrocarbon fuels consist primarily of carbon dioxide, water vapor, oxygen, and nitrogen. If hot enough, the gases may become ionized to produce plasma. The color and intensity of the flame depend on the type of fuel and composition of the surrounding gases."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Large_bonfire.jpg/330px-Large_bonfire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Potjiekos_over_a_fire.gif/500px-Potjiekos_over_a_fire.gif?u